\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N=\{1,2,\ldots\}$; the standard number fields have their usual meanings. All additional conventions are stated locally.


\paragraph{Definitions and conventions.} A finite-energy monopole on $\mathbb R^3$ consists of a connection $A$ and Higgs field $\Phi$ for the gauge group, in the Bogomolny/monopole setting of the source. Framed moduli divide by gauge transformations tending to the identity at infinity. Magnetic charge is determined by the asymptotic Higgs field: one positive integer $k$ for $SU(2)$, or a vector of $N-1$ charges for maximally broken $SU(N)$. The moduli metric is the $L^2$ inner product on infinitesimal field variations perpendicular to gauge directions. The strongly centered $SU(2)$ moduli space removes the center-of-mass translation and total-phase degrees of freedom, with the cover/discrete quotient fixed in the Sen-conjecture convention. Its reduced $L^2$ cohomology is represented by square-integrable harmonic differential forms for this metric. The charge and residual cyclic-group character sectors are relevant to the dimension question, not merely the dimension of ordinary topological cohomology.

\paragraph{Source scope and qualifications.} The report frames this as Sen's conjecture and seeks metric control at infinity. The freshly consulted Fritzsch--Kottke--Singer Part I abstract describes a partial result and explicitly says that a key compactification theorem is deferred to Part II; it is not taken as proof of the whole charge-general conjecture. The brief report does not state every character-sector formula, so none is invented.

\paragraph{Catalogue mathematical target.}
\paragraph{Catalogue wording retained for traceability.}
Determine the dimension of the $L^2$-cohomology of the moduli space of strongly centered $\operatorname{SU}(2)$-monopoles on $\mathbb R^3$.

\paragraph{Saved literature context.} The supplied catalogue's assessment dated 2026-08-21 records: The Sen conjecture for strongly centered SU(2) monopoles has substantial partial results: Fritzsch, Kottke, and Singer prove the coprime case and part of the predicted L2-cohomology statement, but the full charge-general claim is not established. The assessment is retained as dated provenance; it is not a new comprehensive literature or open-status certification.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Determine the square-integrable cohomology dimensions of strongly centered SU(2) monopole moduli spaces.

